#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
# agent-log-shipper — hook collector and log shipper for one agent environment.
#
# Runs as root (systemd unit agent-log-shipper.service) in every agent
# environment: on the host and inside each agent VM.  See
# docs/design/implementation.md, "Hook collector" and "Log shipper".
#
# Threads, each with its own cursor so one stuck source cannot stall the rest:
#
#   collector   /run/agent-log-shipper/hook.sock (mode 0666).  Each hook sends
#               one frame (4-byte big-endian length + JSON).  The collector
#               adds an "observed" object from SO_PEERCRED and /proc, appends
#               {ts, boot_id, observed, event} to the spool, fsyncs, and only
#               then replies "ok".  A single writer thread does all appends.
#   audit-health  every 60 s compares free space under /var/log/audit with
#               auditd's admin_space_left; while below it, the file
#               /run/agent-log-shipper/audit-degraded exists (agent-run
#               refuses to start) and a "meta audit-degraded" record is
#               written.
#
# and, unless --mode local (phase 1: keep records on this machine only):
#
#   hook        reads the spool segments by byte offset
#   journal     `journalctl --all -o json --follow` filtered to the proxy's
#               decisions, kernel drop logs, journald suppression notices,
#               and the pipeline's own logs
#   audit       tails /var/log/audit/audit.log across rotations and groups
#               lines into events
#   transcript  polls ~agent/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl and transcript paths
#               seen in hook records, reading them defensively
#   sender      batches records from all sources to agent-logd (unix socket
#               on the host, vsock CID 2 port 700 from a privileged source
#               port in a VM) and persists cursors only after the ack
#
# Usage:
#   agent-log-shipper --mode host|vm|local [OPTIONS]
#   (see --help; options other than --mode exist for tests and development)
#
# Standard library only; Python >= 3.12.

